### Challenge 3: Client Reconnect Loops

**Problem**: Python client opened new TCP connection for every request

**Observed Behavior**:
```
Client connected
Client disconnected
Client connected
Client disconnected
```

**Root Cause**: Python client was closing socket after each request
```python
# Phase 3 Python client (BAD)
def send_request():
    sock = socket.socket(...)
    sock.connect(...)
    sock.sendall(request)
    sock.close()  # ← Closes connection!
```

**Solution**: ✅ **Persistent connection pattern**
```python
# Phase 4 Python client (GOOD)
sock = socket.socket(...)
sock.connect(...)

# Send multiple requests on SAME socket
sock.sendall(subscribe)
sock.sendall(request1)
sock.sendall(request2)
sock.sendall(unsubscribe)

sock.close()  # Only close at end
```

**Lessons Learned**:
- Test clients should mirror production behavior
- Connection reuse = performance + correctness
- Server must handle both patterns gracefully

